### 6. No CORS Configuration (OWASP A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration)

**Problem:** There's no CORS policy defined. By default, Express won't set CORS headers (so browsers will block cross-origin requests), but this should be explicitly configured to avoid accidentally opening it up later with a permissive `*` wildcard.

**Recommendation:**

```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://your-trusted-frontend.com'],
  methods: ['GET'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true,
}));
```

---

### 7. No Error Handling Middleware (OWASP A09:2021 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures)

**Problem:** There's no global error handler. Unhandled errors will result in Express's default error page, which may leak stack traces and internal details in non-production environments.

**Recommendation:**

```javascript
// Global error handler — place AFTER all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(`[${new Date().toISOString()}] Error:`, err.message);
